# `std::mem::arena` — Regional Bump Arena & 64KB Immix Mark-Region Pool

## 1. Design Intent & Rust `bumpalo` / GC Comparison

In Rust, regional bump allocation (`bumpalo::Bump`) requires `<'a>` lifetime parameters infecting every AST node or parser token (`Node<'a>`), and cyclic graph reclamation requires either `Rc<RefCell<T>>` (which leaks cycles) or external arena index tables.

In Jenny's `std::mem::arena`:
1. **`BumpArena`** provides $O(1)$ 8-byte-aligned bump allocation with `checkpoint()` and `rollback(mark)` for nested parser/compiler scopes, plus `reset()` for zero-cost bulk reclamation.
2. **`ImmixNode` & `ImmixPool`** expose Jenny's **64KB Block (`65,536B`) + 128B Line (`512 lines/block`) Immix Mark-Region Collector** (`^T`):
   - Objects are bump-allocated into free 128B line holes inside 64KB `JnImmixBlock`s.
   - `collect_keep_two(r1, r2)` marks live `^ImmixNode` roots (`jn_gc_begin_mark` + `jn_gc_mark_ptr`), sweeps unmarked 128B lines into reusable holes (`jn_gc_sweep_epoch`), and recycles completely empty 64KB blocks.

## 2. Formal Interface & Contracts

```jenny
module std_mem_arena

import std::rt::intrinsics

pub enum ArenaError {
    OutOfMemory,
    InvalidRequest,
    InvalidWatermark,
}

pub struct BumpArena {
    capacity: i64,
    used: i64 = 0,
    allocs: i64 = 0,
    peak_used: i64 = 0,

    invariant self.capacity >= 64 && self.capacity <= 16777216
    invariant self.used >= 0 && self.used <= self.capacity
    invariant self.allocs >= 0
    invariant self.peak_used >= self.used && self.peak_used <= self.capacity
}

pub struct ImmixNode {
    id: i64,
    payload: i64,
    next: ^ImmixNode?,

    invariant self.id >= 0
}

impl BumpArena {
    pub fn new(capacity: i64) -> BumpArena ! ArenaError
        effects []
        requires capacity >= 64 && capacity <= 16777216 else ArenaError.InvalidRequest
        ensures result.capacity == capacity && result.used == 0 && result.allocs == 0

    pub fn alloc_aligned(mut self, size_bytes: i64) -> i64 ! ArenaError
        effects [Mutate, AllocRegion]
        requires size_bytes > 0 else ArenaError.InvalidRequest
        ensures self.used > old(self.used) && self.allocs == old(self.allocs) + 1

    pub fn checkpoint(self) -> i64
        effects []
        ensures result == self.used

    pub fn rollback(mut self, watermark: i64) -> i64 ! ArenaError
        effects [Mutate]
        requires watermark >= 0 && watermark <= self.used else ArenaError.InvalidWatermark
        ensures self.used == watermark

    pub fn reset(mut self) -> i64
        effects [Mutate]
        ensures self.used == 0 && self.allocs == 0 && self.peak_used >= old(self.peak_used)
}

pub fn immix_spawn_node(id: i64, payload: i64, next: ^ImmixNode?) -> ^ImmixNode
    effects [AllocGC]
    requires id >= 0
    ensures result.id == id && result.payload == payload

pub fn immix_collect_keep_two(r1: ^ImmixNode, r2: ^ImmixNode) -> i64
    effects [AllocGC]
    ensures result >= 0

@example("EX-STD-ARENA-01: BumpArena 8-byte alignment, checkpoint rollback, and bulk reset") {
    var arena = BumpArena.new(1024)!
    val off0 = arena.alloc_aligned(13)!
    assert(off0 == 0)
    assert(arena.used == 16)
    val mark = arena.checkpoint()
    val off1 = arena.alloc_aligned(24)!
    assert(off1 == 16)
    assert(arena.used == 40)
    arena.rollback(mark)!
    assert(arena.used == 16)
    assert(arena.peak_used == 40)
    arena.reset()
    assert(arena.used == 0)
    assert(arena.peak_used == 40)
}

@example("EX-STD-ARENA-02: 64KB Block + 128B Line Immix collector marks live roots and reclaims holes") {
    gc_collect_all()
    val n1 = immix_spawn_node(1, 100, null)
    val n2 = immix_spawn_node(2, 200, n1)
    val dead1 = immix_spawn_node(3, 300, null)
    val dead2 = immix_spawn_node(4, 400, dead1)
    assert(jn_gc_active_blocks() == 1)
    assert(jn_gc_live_lines() == 4)
    val reclaimed = immix_collect_keep_two(n1, n2)
    assert(reclaimed >= 510)
    assert(jn_gc_live_lines() == 2)
    val reused = immix_spawn_node(5, 500, n2)
    assert(reused.payload == 500)
    assert(jn_gc_active_blocks() == 1)
    assert(jn_gc_live_lines() == 3)
    gc_collect_all()
    assert(jn_gc_active_blocks() == 0)
}
```
